platformio (6.2.0-1~ppa2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild from the platformio repository rather than by hand. The
    6.2.0-1~ppa1 debs in the registry were built in October 2026 from a
    packaging tree that no longer exists; this revision is the first one
    that any checkout can reproduce. The source is the same PyPI sdist,
    pinned by sha256 in debian/upstream/sdist.sha256.
  * d/p/relax-deps.patch widens one pip pin: bottle "== 0.13.*" becomes
    ">= 0.12", because noble ships 0.12.25 and PlatformIO's only use of
    bottle is a bottle.template() call that is the same in both. It does
    not change the deb's dependencies -- dh_python3 discards PEP 440
    constraints, measured both ways -- only the requirement metadata the
    installed package records, which otherwise states something noble
    cannot satisfy.
  * Tests stay disabled (PYBUILD_DISABLE=test): upstream's one test module
    downloads toolchains from the network. debian/tests/control covers the
    installed package instead.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0500

platformio (6.2.0-1~ppa1~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of upstream release 6.2.0, from the PyPI sdist, for
    ppa:pillarsdotnet/ppa and the Forgejo registry.
  * Every pip dependency but ajsonrpc is in Ubuntu for all three series;
    python-ajsonrpc is backported separately for noble and resolute.
  * The upstream udev rules install to /usr/lib/udev/rules.d.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Sat, 18 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0400
